TOS Barriers

A barrier synchronizes N threads at a rendezvous point.
All threads call barrier_wait; none proceeds until all N
have arrived. The barrier then resets for reuse.

    module oskit

Uses a generation counter to allow reuse. Each call to
barrier_wait increments the arrival count. The last thread
to arrive resets the count and posts the semaphore N-1 times
to release the others. Waiting threads block on the semaphore
until released.

    struct Barrier
        target: i64
        count: i64
        generation: i64
        sem: i64

    barrier_sem(b: i64) -> *i64
        *i64(b + 24)

    barrier_init(b: *Barrier, n: i64)
        b.target = n
        b.count = 0
        b.generation = 0
        val addr: i64 = i64(b)
        sem_init(barrier_sem(addr), 0)

    barrier_wait(b: *Barrier)
        val addr: i64 = i64(b)
        val gen = b.generation
        b.count += 1
        if b.count == b.target
            b.count = 0
            b.generation += 1
            var i: i64 = 1
            while i < b.target
                sem_post(barrier_sem(addr))
                i += 1
        else
            while b.generation == gen
                sem_wait(barrier_sem(addr))
